# Rescue and diablerie, actions of their own (rulebook, "Rescue a Vampire from Torpor", "Diablerize
# a Vampire in Torpor", "The Blood Hunt"; zero-vtes docs/rules-digest.md §11.6, §11.7, checked at
# 1f33be5). A ready vampire acts on a vampire in torpor: directed at its controller when it's
# another Methuselah's, undirected when it's your own (rules-qa 16.4). A rescue costs 2 blood as it
# succeeds, shared as announced (48.8); a share its payer can't meet, or the vampire out of torpor,
# fizzles it: successful, no effect (3.6, 28.7). A diablerie's blood hunt comes inside the action,
# its after-resolution window after (5.8); out of torpor by then, it fizzles with no blood hunt.
# Alice plays first: her prey is Bob, her predator Carol.
seed 28
seat A alice
seat B bob
seat C carol
crypt A "Vera Nightfall" *12
library A "Iron Ward" *40
crypt B "Marek Hale" *12
library B "Iron Ward" *40
crypt C "Odile Fen" *12
library C "Iron Ward" *40
start

# Fast-forward: Alice has three vampires, one in torpor; Bob two, one in torpor; Carol one.
A> transfer +3 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> transfer +1 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> transfer +2 A:uncontrolled:1
A> move A:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> move A:ready:3 torpor
B> transfer +3 B:uncontrolled:1
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
B> transfer +2 B:uncontrolled:1
B> move B:uncontrolled:1 ready
B> move B:ready:2 torpor
C> move C:uncontrolled:1 ready
A> next
A> next
expect turn 1 A minion

# Rescuing her own vampire is undirected: Bob (prey) and Carol (predator) may block. The rescued
# vampire pays 1 of the 2 blood, the rescuer the other.
A> rescue A:ready:1 A:torpor:1 1
log public A: Vera Nightfall tries to rescue Vera Nightfall, Vera Nightfall paying 1 blood
expect action rescue A blocks
B> pass
C> pass
A> resolve success
log public The action succeeded
expect count A:torpor 0
expect count A:ready 3
expect card A:ready:1 blood 2
expect card A:ready:3 blood 1
A> pass
expect action none

# Rescuing Bob's vampire is directed at him: only Bob may block. Alice's second vampire, with 1
# blood, would pay both: it can't, so the rescue fizzles (48.8, 3.6).
A> rescue A:ready:2 B:torpor:1
expect action rescue A blocks
B> pass
A> resolve success
log public The action succeeded
expect count B:torpor 1
expect card A:ready:2 blood 1
A> pass

# Diablerizing Bob's vampire, also directed at him. It succeeds: its 2 blood go to the diablerist,
# the victim burns, and the blood hunt follows at once, polled from Alice.
A> unlock A:ready:1
A> diablerie A:ready:1 B:torpor:1
log public A: Vera Nightfall tries to diablerize Marek Hale
B> pass
A> resolve success
log public Vera Nightfall diablerizes Marek Hale, taking 2 blood
expect card A:ready:1 blood 4
expect count B:torpor 0
expect window polling minion
A> pass
B> vote against B:ready:1
B> pass
C> pass
A> pass
# The hunt fails (none for, a prince's 2 votes against); the action succeeded, and its
# after-resolution window opens after the blood hunt.
log public No blood hunt (0 for, 2 against)
expect action diablerie A after
A> pass
expect action none

# Bob sends his other vampire to torpor; Alice's third goes after it. Before it resolves, the
# vampire leaves torpor: the diablerie fizzles, no blood hunt (28.7).
B> move B:ready:1 torpor
A> diablerie A:ready:3 B:torpor:1
B> pass
B> move B:torpor:1 ready
A> resolve success
log public The action succeeded
expect count B:ready 1
expect window after-resolution minion
